    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0bcab421",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the meme's accusatory text and visual juxtaposition",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's textual and visual elements that create a false and hateful accusation. The top text 'Claims that her ancestors created a safe space for Jews' and the bottom text 'these are her ancestors' are directed at the viewer, implying the viewer is the one making the accusation or is being asked to accept the false narrative. The visual juxtaposition of the modern speaker with Hitler and the woman is presented as evidence, projecting the user into the role of someone who must confront or judge the speaker based on this false historical connection. The meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the accusatory framing and the implication that the viewer is engaging with this false narrative project the user onto the meme's core message and visual evidence.",
